      ],
      "text": "Bronchiectasis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ICS if complicated by asthma or ABPA; they may increase infection risk in patients without a clear indication."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated as primary treatment of status asthmaticus or acute asthma needing intensive measures. Caution: can worsen TB, fungal, bacterial, viral, parasitic or ocular HSV infection; chickenpox/measles can be severe or fatal in non-immune patients. Switching from oral steroids: risk of adrenal insufficiency, taper the systemic steroid slowly."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Fluticasone is a CYP3A4 substrate:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ketoconazole) raise exposure; use caution."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
